    <div class="headerImage2">
        <img src="~/images/consultants.jpeg" />
    </div>
}
<div class="bgEmployibility5Top">
</div>
<div class="hometext bgEmployibility5">


    <div class="">
        <ul class="ulBreadcrumb" style="padding-top:10px;">
            <li><a href="/">Home <span class="fa fa-angle-right"></span></a></li>
            <li><a href="/home/employability_index">Employability Index<span class="fa fa-angle-right"></span></a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="paraCommon paraHeader"><b>Ethical Policy: How Career DNA Outputs Are Shared with Employers</b></p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            www.greenjobs.digital follows a candidate-first, consent-driven approach to sharing Career DNA insights. Our principles are simple:
            <ul>
               
                <li><b>Ownership:</b> Career DNA belongs to the individual, not the platform and not the employer. </li>
                <li><b>Consent:</b> No Career DNA output is shared with any employer without explicit, informed permission from the candidate. </li>
                <li><b>Transparency:</b> Candidates can see exactly what is being shared and why. </li>
                <li><b>Context, not scores:</b> Employers can request for interpretive insights like strength areas, growth themes, readiness signals - not raw conversations, transcripts, or hidden scores. </li>
                <li><b>No black-box filtering:</b> Career DNA is never used for automated rejection or exclusion. </li>

            </ul>
           
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">
            Employers are encouraged to use Career DNA outputs as:
            <ul>
                <li>Conversation starters</li>
                <li>Onboarding guides</li>
                <li>Learning and mentoring inputs</li>
            </ul>
           
        </p>
        <p class="paraCommon">Not as mechanical hiring decisions. </p>
       
        <p class="paraCommon">  </p>

    </div>
    <p class="paraCommon"> </p>
</div>
